Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-25-1999||01:54 AM||||I have an idea for a mod and could use some input.  Here goes:  Later model Camaro p/mirrors mounted on the body where they belong (why would Pontiac mount the mirrors on the doors and leave that mt space on the body?-Probably the same idiot who decided to kill the Fiero!).  I know this isn't a new idea.  But, I have inner door skins with the manual mirrors (joystick control).  I am building a custom dash and I don't want to clutter it up with too many extra switches.  Here's my idea:  Use a p/mirror control from a mid-'80s Escort (yuck) in place of the joystick I now have.  My mother had one on a car once and it seems like it would be a perfect fit.  Still a joystick control.  You know, you move it the same to control the mirrors and twist it for left or right side control.  This seems fairly straight forward, but I just need to know if the wiring would connect.  I know it wouldn't be a plug-n-play deal, but couldn't I splice some wires together to make it work?  I think I can get the mirrors for about $30/set.  Is that a good price?  The controller is $43 brand new from Ford.  Also, are there any wire for p/mirrors already in a Fiero that didn't have them from the factory? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||11-25-1999||11:33 AM||||There is no power mirror wiring present. I have installed many power mirror options in cars that originally didnt have them. I think this is easier that trying to get a bunch of parts that dont belong together to work together. But I could be completely wrong. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-25-1999||01:33 PM||||check the arc of the door and window edge as it opens. You have to make sure a body mount mirror dosn't obstruct the window when you open the door.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-26-1999||12:13 AM||||ogre--I thought about that and I will definitely double check, but I read/saw somewhere (maybe this forum?) that somebody had already done it with those mirrors.  Also, I have a pic (off the net) with body mtd mirrors.  Thanx for your advice, though.||||reg||1
